  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### sl(3) Gaudin L = 2 chain result (2026-10-16)\n\n**Symbolic Hamiltonians** (column-ordered cdet(dd - L_g), normal-ordered once on 27 symbols): S1 = l11+l22+l33; **S2 = Σ_{i<j}(l_ii l_jj - l_ji l_ij) - l'22 - 2 l'33**; **S3 = l''33 - l11 l'33 - l22 l'33 - l'22 l33 + l31 l'13 + l32 l'23 + l'32 l23 + l11 l22 l33 - l11 l32 l23 - l21 l12 l33 + l21 l32 l13 + l31 l12 l23 - l31 l22 l13** (ordered products). No variant was needed: the plan's convention works at the first attempt: [S_a(u), S_b(v)] = 0 exactly (7 pairs), S1 scalar, weight conserved, for both Λ. Laurent data (exact fits, verified at extra points): S3 has NO triple pole (coefficient exactly 0), S2 double poles = 3 ([2,1,0]), S_k(∞) = e_k(ζ). **Sign difference to the plan**: Res_{θ1} S2 = H1 = -[Σ ζ_i E1_ii + Σ_ik E1_ik E2_ki/θ12] + (|Λ|Σζ + |Λ|²/θ12) id exactly (the plan expected +), and H1 + H2 = -W + 2|Λ|Σζ (plan: +W).\n\n**Bra vacuum**: Ω⊗Ω = ΩD[ζ,ω]⊗ΩD[ζ,ω] is the exact left eigencovector of S2^{(g')}, S3^{(g')} at u0, u1 for g' = PauxG[ζ].gc[ω].PauxG[ζ]^-1 (variant V1) at P, P' and a regime point; the variants with inverse conjugation and the transposes, and the control diag(ω), fail. One-site statement: M = rows = left eigenvectors of g' (ω order, first entry 1) gives ΩD[ζ,ω] = e1 ρ(U-factor of **M^{-T}**) exactly (M, M^-1, M^T give wrong covectors). P_phys^G(ζ) = (PauxG^-1)^T exactly; x0G (= XXX x0Of with z->ζ) has all components nonzero; min |x0G.Ψ_B| = 3.2e-5 over the 64 G-normalised states at P ([2,1,0]). ΩD[εφ, εω̂] and the undone covector φ_u are exactly ε-independent. All 64 (S2(u0), S3(u1)) pairs are real and distinct at P and P' (table in the cell \"The 64 eigenvalue pairs\").\n\n**Localisers (which T's), exact at P and P'**: D1 = span{id, W, H1, S3c[1,2], S3c[1,1], S3c[2,2], S3c[2,1]} has rank 7; D2 = D1 + quadratic monomials has rank 24 ([2,1,0]) / 26 ([3,1,0]); the span of cubic monomials has rank 48 / 68 (NOT 64: not vacuous). [2,1,0]: ℓ1 = ℓ2 = 3 already inside D1 (no products needed; unchanged for D1+H1.D1, D2 and cubic). **Site 1: X ∈ {id, H1, S3c[1,2]}, each separately** (H1 = Res_{θ1} S2, S3c[1,2] = coefficient of (u-θ1)^-2 in S3); **site 2: {id, W+H1 (= -H2 + scalar), S3c[2,2]}**. Identification: ⟨Ω⊗Ω|id = Ω1⊗Ω1; ⟨Ω⊗Ω|H1 = [Ω1(|Λ|Σζ + 4/θ12 - C_ζ)]⊗Ω1 (P: 1831/124 = 41/4 + 4·35/31; P': 869/62, checked); ⟨Ω⊗Ω|S3c[1,2] = [Ω1·S3^{1-site}[-2]]⊗Ω1 exactly (S3^{1-site}[-2] = (u-θ1)^-2 coefficient of the one-site cdet with twist diag ζ); site 2: same pattern with +C_ζ and θ2 one-site coefficients. So **L1 = Ω1·span{1, C_ζ, S3^{1-site}[-2]}, ℓ1 = ℓ2 = 3**, covering every weight of V (ranks = weight dimensions). Spectator factors f = ⟨Ω⊗Ω|X|e1⊗e1⟩ (v normalised to first component 1) as exact Laurent polynomials in θ12 (fit on 6 values, 3 checks): [2,1,0] at P: f(H1) = 6 + 4/θ12, f(S3c12) = 2, f(H2) = 6 - 4/θ12, f(S3c22) = 2; at P': f(H1) = 23/6 + 4/θ12, f(S3c12) = -3/2. [3,1,0] at P: f(H1) = 95/12 + 6/θ12, f(S3c12) = 8/3; P': f(H1) = 5 + 6/θ12, f(S3c12) = -2. **[3,1,0]: ℓ1 = 3 over D1 but 4 over D1 + H1.D1 and over D2 and cubic (site 2: 3 over D1 + H1.D1, 4 over D2): one extra localiser from quadratic products (ℓ = λ1+1 = 4, matching the XXX count); no single product completes it (0 of 19 tried), so it needs at least 2 products; its explicit form was NOT identified. The 4-dim L lies inside Ω1·(one-site operators and their pair products) but not inside Ω1·(one-site operators) alone (ranks 4 vs 5, see the cell 'Which T's localise').** The predicted localiser X1 = -(4631/124) id + 3 H1 - S3c[1,2] from the Python side is reproduced exactly ([2,1,0], cross-check cell): ⟨Ω⊗Ω|X1 = u⊗Ω1 with u = Ω1(431/62 - 3C_ζ - S3^{1-site}[-2]) (a linear combination of my three separate localisers). The other P1/P2 cross-checks (S3 no triple pole, S2 double pole 3, S_k(∞) = e_k, vacuum S2 eigenvalue function, vacuum S3 double poles 9/5 and 27/7) agree exactly.\n\n**Eigenstates**: HW-limit branches at ζ = εφ (ε = 1,2,4 e-6): raising residual ≤ 6.6e-7 vs ≥ 1.3 for the rest; deviation from the exact untwisted HW state ∝ ε (exponent 1.000) in every sector, including the multiplicity-2 ones. Multiplicity-2 HW spaces ([3,2,1] for [2,1,0]; [5,2,1], [4,3,1] for [3,1,0]): S2(u0) is a SCALAR there (91189/432 for [3,2,1]), so S3 splits the copies; the matrix of S3c[1,2] for [3,2,1] is (105/62)[[3,-1],[-1,7]] with eigenvalues 12.2546, 4.6809 and the same eigenvectors as S3(u1) (they commute); the untwisted copies (HW-ket coefficients printed) = eigenvectors of S3c[1,2] (copy 1 <-> smaller eigenvalue).\n\n**K/S table (Task 4c)**: K/S = O(ε) for EVERY HW branch, both reps, main family (24 points): max|K/S| at ε = 1,2,4 e-6 doubles (ratios 2.000, 2.000); K = 0 for the top branch; S = O(1) (ε-exponent 0 for all, since the Gaudin vacua are ε-free and the Ψ_B are G-normalised). [2,1,0] max|K/S| at 1e-6: 4.9e-7 (4,1,1), 2.4e-6 (3,3,0), 2.4e-6 and 1.6e-6 (3,2,1 copies 1,2), 5.4e-6 (2,2,2); [3,1,0] up to 7.7e-6 (3,3,2). Singlet and both octets included. Undo S = ⟨φ_u⊗e1|P_HWΨ⟩ to 1e-193.\n\n**CG table (Task 4d)**: overlap-extracted C = R_C/φ_u[slice] equals the chain slice with error ∝ ε (ratio 4.00 between 4e-6 and 1e-6), spread over the grid ∝ ε; the Richardson limits reproduce the exact G-norm-1 HW-ket slices to 1e-19 .. 1e-17 relative (1-dim slices for [2,1,0]: -1/√2, -1/√2, 0.1178511302; 2-dim slices solved from pairs of grid points: octet 1 = (0.04931160001, 0.2088872897), octet 2 = (0.3379867346, -0.07978784486)), including the octet mixing R_c = (e1E13.C)/(e1E23E12.C): exact 5.854101966250 and -0.854101966250 (roots of R² - 5R - 5 = 0), overlap-extracted agree to 1.5e-18 / 5.7e-20 relative; [3,1,0], (5,2,1): 4.311737691490 and -0.811737691490 (agree to 5e-19); the (4,3,1) mixing needs other functionals and was not computed. φ_u closed forms (a', c', g') equal the XXX leading coefficients exactly, Jacobian rank 3, per-weight ranks over the 24-point grid = weight multiplicity (CG-complete) for both reps. **Controls**: common ω1' = ω1 gives a' = g' = 0 and reads only the branches (4,2,0), (4,1,1) ([2,1,0]), the others are \"not read\", as expected; **ω' fixed (7/4,-2/5): the XXX-motivated expectation is REFUTED in Gaudin**: ΩD[ζ -> 0, ω'] has a finite direction-dependent limit, K/S is still O(ε) for every branch, S still O(1), all slices are extracted with the same quality, per-weight ranks of the limit φ_u over 6 directions are full. A genuinely degenerate control (both ω, ω' fixed) was not run.\n\n**Q-side numbers (Task 4f)** at one grid point: ⟨Ω_ω⊗Ω_ω|Ψ⟩ and ⟨Ω_ω'⊗Ω_ω'|Ψ⟩ are ∝ ε (exponent 1.0; ε² for the singlet), the mixed ⟨Ω_ω⊗Ω_ω'|Ψ⟩ = -⟨Ω_ω'⊗Ω_ω|Ψ⟩ (octets, (4,1,1), (3,3,0)) are O(1); the reference overlap ⟨Ω_{ω0}^{⊗2}|Ψ⟩ with ω0 = ε(2/5,1/7) is ∝ ε (ε² for the singlet).\n\n**Surprises / not done**: (i) the sign of the H1 and W relations vs the plan; (ii) cubic span rank 48/68 rather than 64; (iii) the ω'-fixed control does not fail; (iv) [3,1,0] fourth (quadratic) localiser not identified; (v) mixing for the (4,3,1) sector not computed; (vi) the kernel was restarted once during the build (a stuck run), all cells were then rerun from the first cell.\n",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
